# `push_batch_within`'s attempt counter, stuck at zero.
#
# `attempt *= 1` never advances from its initial zero, so the budget bound never
# fires and the loop is held together entirely by its `moved == 0` break. That
# break does fire, which is why this survived a suite that watches only the
# published count of an ordinary iterator. But against a source that yields one
# burst per attempt (see S7) it fires only once the ring is full, bursts past
# the budget.
#
# The detector's ring refuses rather than drops, and that is load-bearing. A
# full `Fail` ring makes the next attempt move nothing, which fires the break.
# Under `DropNewest` every attempt reports its burst as moved, the break never
# fires, and against an endless source this mutation is an infinite loop.

id: S9
crate: ring_poll
file: src/lib.rs
round: 2026-10-01
round-failures: 1
detector: push_batch_within_spends_its_whole_budget_while_attempts_keep_moving_records

--- from
      break;
    }
    attempt += 1;
--- to
      break;
    }
    attempt *= 1;   // PROBE ONLY — G12, was `+=`
--- end
